{"agent":"sw-remoteauth","data":{"body":"Fixes bug B-token-role-widened-by-project-config: [agent].roles and [agent].capability_verbs are read from every layer, including the committed project config, so a token holder with `merge` (default bot and agent roles) can land a config change that gives its own role `*`. services/auth trusts cfg as loaded. P-remote.security requires that a cloned project cannot widen a role; which layers may set these two tables is an operator decision (r-tighten-only). Local same-user processes can already edit config, so this bites once P-remote.serve makes a role a real boundary. Found on P-remote.security.\n\nWrite the regression test first and watch it FAIL on the unfixed code; then `ddflow complete fix-B-token-role-widened-by-project-config --regression-test <test>` closes the bug with the task (or `ddflow bug fixed B-token-role-widened-by-project-config --regression-test <test>` first).\n\nNot attached, they match nothing in the tree: tests/test_remote_threats.py, docs/ddflow/decisions/remote-threats.md.","fixes":["B-token-role-widened-by-project-config"],"globs":[],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"bugs-2","priority":50,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Fix bug B-token-role-widened-by-project-config: A committed project config can widen what a paired token may do"},"id":"e15ad545edb97ec189ec4a425","kind":"task.added","lamport":139623,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-token-role-widened-by-project-config","ts":"2026-11-05T12:48:41.226578Z"}
